General Liability Coverage Extensions - 
Contractual Liability Coverage - Coverage Supplement

Amendments of   Care, Custody or Control Exclusion.  The ISO/AC
 Contractual    Broad Form Property Damage Endorsement may be
 Coverage       amended by adding the words "Contrctual Liability
 (Cont.)        Insurance" in the coverage identification box to
        extend the coverage to Contractual Coverage Parts.
        To be eligible for the amendments, the Comprehen-
        sive General Liability must be similarly endorsed.
        
 Underwriting   Underwriting Contractul Liability involves all
  Summary       the words of the contractual agreement and an
        analysis of the actual operations of both the
        potential insured and the organization trans-
        ferring its liability; all of this related to the
        insurance coverage.
        
        An aid to the underwriting process, Contractual
        Profile, is attached (Exhibit 1).
        
 PRICING        Contractual Liability coverage is judgement rated
        excet for certain classifications of contracts in
        the ISO Commercial Lines manual.
        
        When the risk is a contractor, CLUG 9 or 0, or
        exposures are greater that normal, the initial
        rates for Extension Endorsements and blanket
        coverage are contained in the Guide Liability
        Rates section of these procedures.
        
        For other Situations, Extension Endorsement rating
        includes charges for the coverage in the single
        percentage rate.
        
        Amendments of contractual coverage.  Adjust the
        following minimum guide charges upward for greater
        exposures:
        
        + Delete Sole Negligence Exclusion - use the
          rate differential in the Guide Liability Rates.
        
        + Delete Railroad Exclusion - Rate the contract
          individually, or, if no exposure exists, no
          charge.  When there is an exposure, be sure
          to get O&CP charges, specific railroad
          contract charges, and look for railroad
          protective requirements.
          
        + Broad Form Property Damage endorsement - See
          amended Care, Custody and Control section of 
          these procedures.

Broad Form
 Property               INITIAL RATE-COMPLETED OP'S
 Damage         RISK CLASS      EXCLUDED        INCLUDED
 Endorsement
        IC15XXX-17XXX   15%     20%
        40XXX-47XXX     15%*    *
        
        Other IC's      
        with completed
        operations
        exposure        15%     20%
        
        IC's with no
        completed Op's  5-10%   5-15%

        Percentage rates are appllied to the property
        damage premiums for the risk, excluding or
        including the products/completed operations
        premium according to the coverage selected.  A
        $20.00 basic limits minimum premium applies.
        
        *There is a coverage overlap with cargo libility.
        Broad Form Property Damage coverage should be 
        discouraged and if required, only coverage
        excluding completed operations should be
        extended.
        
        **There are judgement rates and rates should be 
        adjusted when exposures vary.  Rates of 40% are
        not unheard of.
        
        When the Broad Form Property endorsement is to
        apply to Contractual Liability, "Contractual
        Liability Insurance" must be typed in the Coverage
        Identification section and the Contractual
        Liability premium included in the base for premium 
        computation.
        
        The enabling rule to support the pricing is
        contained in the Supplementary Rules to the
        Commercial Lines Manual.

